    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but finding \"joy\" in the process feels like such a cope, doesn't it? it's just a way to distract ourselves from the fact that there's no objective ground to stand on. if the universe doesn't care and nothing we do actually leaves a permanent mark, then the struggle to keep going feels less like \"finding joy\" and more like just prolonging an inevitable decay. it's exhausting to pretend there's a point when logically, there isn't one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
